WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.280
this task workflow,

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:08.680
I think showbit actually already has a video here. So, this could be useful to watch the

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:09.440
whole task end

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.140
to end.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.020
But you claim a task on Handshake. You install the CLI tool that we provide to you.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:24.060
So, this should help you through the task. You, once you install the CLI tool,

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.380
you set up the task. So, you'll read the task. You

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:37.460
will... Sorry, I'm just moving zoom.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.060
You read the task. You'll set up your environment.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.920
And your environment is basically like your Docker

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.180
file.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.600
Obviously, you make sure that you set up your assistant AI before in Opencode.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:00.460
So, then you'll run arm A. You'll run arm A.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.940
And you will, when you run arm A, the first thing that

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:09.240
you do is you annotate arm A. So, you run arm A. I think we can clarify this in the instructions as

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.360
well. So, you don't run arm A and arm B. What you'll do is, this is actually super important,

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:19.880
is you'll run arm A. So, you kick off that run. Then

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.260
you will go and you'll submit it. You'll

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:30.100
basically open a PR. And you will have an automated quality check

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.820
that will automatically check your

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:37.740
first run. Once that's approved, you then fill out your ratings.json

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.760
file for arm A. And you also

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:46.520
fill out your behavioral

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:52.240
issues.json file for arm A. Then you submit that. Then another quality check

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.400
will... So, you basically push to the PR. Then another quality check will trigger. After that,

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:02.860
you do the same thing for arm B. So, you run arm B. You run the model through arm B.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:03.860
You

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:04.680
submit it.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:11.760
Quality check runs. You do your ratings.json file and your behavioral issues.json

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.240
file

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:18.060
for arm B. Submit. Quality check runs. And then you do one final

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.460
comparison.json file.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:28.320
And then you submit that. So, you'll open the PR. And then you'll have four more pushes,

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.760
basically, after that. And you'll have quality check that runs in between each of those.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.420
So, I would wait till the quality check passes before you move to the next step. This should

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.140
make it easier for you so you don't do all the work at once. And then the quality check runs.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.740
And then it says that you did something wrong at the beginning. And then you have to start all

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.940
again. So, if you do it sequentially, it should make things a lot easier for you. So,

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:53.640
you don't have to do a bunch of work again that you messed up at the beginning.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:00.160
So, I think we can clarify all these things in the instructions that should already be in here.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.240
These automated checks.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.640
So, all these else should be in here. So, if you have any questions,

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.680
we can go over that now.
